# Lombok

Do not hand-write getters, setters, `equals`/`hashCode`/`toString`, or boilerplate constructors. Use Lombok.

Match existing project style:

- `@Value` — immutable DTOs / models (preferred over `record` here)
- `@RequiredArgsConstructor` — classes whose fields are `final` dependencies
- `@Getter` — mutable types that still need accessors
- `@AllArgsConstructor(access = AccessLevel.PRIVATE)` — when a static factory owns construction

```java
// Bad
public final class ActivityBox {
    private final int wid;
    public ActivityBox(int wid) { this.wid = wid; }
    public int wid() { return wid; }
}

// Good
@Value
public class ActivityBox {
    int wid;
}
```

Keep real methods (domain helpers, factories like `from(...)`, merge logic). Only drop the boilerplate accessors/ctors Lombok already generates.
